# Vietnamese History Glossary

Reusable proper-noun glossary for translating Vietnamese historical/documentary texts, especially those covering the First Indochina War period (1945-1954), the Bình Xuyên organization, and Southern Vietnamese underworld figures.

## People

| Vietnamese | Keep-as (English) | Notes |
|-----------|-------------------|-------|
| Lê Văn Viễn (Bảy Viễn) | Bay Vien (Le Van Vien) | Main figure; leader of Bình Xuyên, "Viễn the Seventh" |
| Dương Văn Dương (Ba Dương) | Ba Duong (Duong Van Duong) | Founder of Bình Xuyên, posthumous Major General, killed 1946 |
| Huỳnh Văn Trí (Mười Trí) | Muoi Tri (Huynh Van Tri) | Bay Vien's sworn brother, stayed with Việt Minh |
| Ngô Đình Diệm | Ngo Dinh Diem | Prime Minister/President of South Vietnam, antagonist |
| Bảo Đại | Bao Dai | Emperor/Chief of State, Bay Vien's patron |
| Nguyễn Bình | Nguyen Binh | Việt Minh Lieutenant General, Commander of War Zone 7 |
| Pierre Darcourt | Pierre Darcourt | French journalist who wrote "Bay Vien: le maître de Cholon" |
| Nguyên Hùng | Nguyen Hung | Author of "Bảy Viễn — Thủ Lĩnh Bình Xuyên" |
| Dương Văn Minh | Duong Van Minh | VNA General who crushed Bình Xuyên in 1955 |
| Trần Văn Giàu | Tran Van Giau | Việt Minh Cochinchina chief |
| Võ Văn Môn (Bảy Môn) | Bay Mon (Vo Van Mon) | Bình Xuyên battalion commander |
| Dương Văn Hà (Năm Hà) | Nam Ha (Duong Van Ha) | Ba Duong's half-brother |
| Maurice Thiên (Tư Thiên) | Maurice Thien / Tu Thien | French-Chinese adviser, casino operator |
| Savani (Antoine-Marie Savani) | Savani | French SDECE/Deuxième Bureau intelligence officer |
| François-Xavier Franchini | Franchini | Continental Hotel owner, Corsican, Bay Vien ally |
| Ngô Đình Nhu | Ngo Dinh Nhu | Diem's brother, secret police chief |
| Phạm Công Tắc | Pham Cong Tac | Pope of Cao Đài |
| Huỳnh Phú Sổ | Huynh Phu So | Founder of Hòa Hảo |
| Lê Quang Vinh (Ba Nhỏ) | Ba Nho (Le Quang Vinh) | Bình Xuyen warlord executed by Nguyen Binh |
| Trần Văn Ân | Tran Van An | Revolutionary intellectual, Bình Xuyên advisor |
| Hồ Hữu Tường | Ho Huu Tuong | Political intellectual |

